    {
      "id": "exhaustive-exploration-sound",
      "kind": "invariant",
      "statement": "Exhaustive exploration within stated bounds finds the known race of a fixture protocol with a counterexample run that Lean accepts, reports its fixed version as holding for all N explored configurations, and gives the same N on every run.",
      "rationale": "The explorer is defined and proved in Lean (formal/Exegra/Explore.lean, WG-4696): explore_sound and explore_counterexample_real build with only Lean's standard axioms, pinned with #guard_msgs. The test runs exegra prove on tests/fixtures/race: the read-modify-write store's lost update, which its scripted run does not show, is found as a counterexample; the atomic store is verified for all N configurations, the same N on two runs. Each result is a theorem discharged by native_decide, so it also trusts the Lean compiler. The Rust explorer (WG-4650) is planned and will be checked differentially against this one. Exegra records the test as evidence; it does not check the proofs itself.",
      "subjects": [
        "exhaustive-explorer",
        "simulation-engine"
