      "kind": "invariant",
      "statement": "exegra prove on a format-2 scenario reports the seed first, and the scope \"fault times fixed as declared\" when the scenario has windowed faults, and shows a result as verified only when the engine input contains no distribution other than fixed or choice anywhere and no element that draws (no Poisson process; no batch, think, closed start, population start.at, emit size or after, timer delay or restartAfter other than fixed or choice; no uniform client pick, groups, choose or sample payload field, or random route), a check made statically on the input; choice values and any routes are enumerated as nondeterminism.",
      "rationale": "Planned (WG-4664, WG-4715; the criterion is stated once in docs/simulation.md, Exploration and sampling). Negative twin: a fixture that is fixed everywhere except one emit size drawn from a uniform distribution must not be shown as verified; the same fixture with that size fixed, and a route changed from random to any, must be, after the explorer enumerates every instance. Not evaluated until recorded evidence exists.",
